{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaRnQRfa4M5YPdBLWojw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the `sorry` in `Main.lean` with a proof, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem plus_eq_add (n m : Nat) : plus n m = n + m := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => rfl\n  | succ m ih => simp [plus, ih, Nat.add_assoc]\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on `m`, the argument that `plus` recurses on:\n- **When `m` is 0:** `plus n 0` reduces to `n` by definition, and `n + 0` also reduces to `n`, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **When `m` is `m + 1`:** unfolding `plus` gives `plus n m + 1`. The induction hypothesis turns that into `n + m + 1`, which equals `n + (m + 1)` by associativity."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":7857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9debc2dd-b903-449f-a806-d13ce94bd56a","uuid":"7bbe9caf-b8ff-4d30-b8ff-5dc042481656","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:54:31.990Z","request_id":"req_011CgaRnPwfBj1jcnhvmkf8J"}
